{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Advanced 7 \u00b7 Modulating the modulators",
 "text": "A patch where one LFO wobbles the filter (a wah) and a second, much slower LFO changes how fast the first one goes (its RATE input): the wah speeds up and slows down by itself over about ten seconds. Modulating a modulator (its rate, or its depth through a VCA as in Advanced 1) is how patches stay alive instead of repeating mechanically. Watch the first LFO's trace speed up and slow down.\n\nTry: the slow LFO's RATE; the first LFO's RATE MOD (how much the slow one changes it); an envelope into the first LFO's RATE instead (a wobble that speeds up on every note); MIDI In's MOD WHEEL into it (you play the speed); the first LFO's WAVE (Square: a rhythmic chop whose tempo drifts).",
